Hecks.hecksagon "StalePr" do
  # stale-pr-recheck-rebase (sprint 20) — HONESTLY BLOCKED, not faked.
  #
  # The three seams (re-check pr_mergeable at Approve ; bounce a stale PR ;
  # auto-rebase open PRs when main moves) each need a runtime feature that
  # does not exist yet, so NO adapter is wired — a wired dispatch here would
  # either fake success (canned Tools::Cascade.RecordResult, a no-op) or fire
  # an UNCONDITIONAL MergeQueue.FailMerge on every StoryApproved (which, now
  # that resolver-on-cascade is live, would bounce EVERY approved PR as
  # "stale base"). Both are removed.
  #
  # Real implementation is gated on, in order :
  #   conditional-dispatch          — the DSL has no branch ; re-check vs.
  #                                   bounce is a probe-gated decision.
  #   hex-invocation-principle      — live staleness probe (gh pr view +
  #                                   git merge-base base..origin/main).
  #   runtime-cross-aggregate-where — fan-out to all open PRs
  #                                   (Plan::Story.ReadyForReview by branch).
  # When conditional-dispatch + the live-probe land, the re-check becomes an
  # inline live-check leaf (cf. pr_mergeable_check.hecksagon) gated on its
  # result. Until then this file is documentation, not behaviour.
end
